{"content": [{"text": "I'll work through this problem independently and check the answer against each rubric criterion.\n\n## Independent computation\n\nI need to count length-7 strings over {0,...,9} with digit sum exactly 30 and no two adjacent digits equal. I'll use DP over (position, running sum, previous digit). Let me set this up carefully via a generating-function-friendly approach.\n\nLet me define the count via the transfer structure. The total without the adjacency constraint is the coefficient of $x^{30}$ in... but I need adjacency. Let me do the DP by hand systematically. This is large, so I'll organize it by tracking, for each position, a distribution over (sum, last digit). That's too much by hand directly, so let me use a smarter decomposition.\n\n**Strategy: inclusion-exclusion on adjacency.** Let $U$ = number of length-7 sequences in $\\{0..9\\}^7$ with sum 30 (no adjacency constraint). For the adjacency constraint, I use inclusion-exclusion over the set of \"bad\" equalities at the 6 adjacent boundaries. Merging $k$ chosen boundaries into runs: if we force equalities on a subset $S$ of the 6 boundaries, the sequence breaks into $7-|S|$ blocks, each block being a run of equal digits. A block of length $\\ell$ contributes a digit $d$ with value $\\ell \\cdot d$ to the sum, where $d \\in \\{0..9\\}$.\n\nSo with sign $(-1)^{|S|}$, the answer is\n$$\\sum_{S} (-1)^{|S|} \\cdot [\\text{# ways to assign digits to the } 7-|S| \\text{ blocks so total} = 30].$$\n\nThe blocks have lengths determined by the composition of 7 induced by $S$ (an ordered composition since boundaries are positional). For a given composition $(\\ell_1,...,\\ell_m)$ of 7 with $m = 7-|S|$ parts, $|S| = 7-m$, sign $(-1)^{7-m}$. The count is the coefficient of $x^{30}$ in $\\prod_i \\left(\\sum_{d=0}^{9} x^{\\ell_i d}\\right)$.\n\nLet me define $f_\\ell(x) = \\sum_{d=0}^9 x^{\\ell d} = 1 + x^\\ell + x^{2\\ell} + \\dots + x^{9\\ell}$, the generating function for one block of length $\\ell